## Lecture 5.2 -- Containerizing Frontend

# The point of this is to prepare a container that is built, then served with nginx

# Once the prep of the Dockerfile and .dockerignore:

docker build -t blog-frontend .

# Docker command for run frontend...

docker run -it -p 3000:80 blog-frontend

# Docker compose uses a .yml file to define all containers to run with arguments

# Docker compose up starts all containers, arguments

docker compose up
